Z||000000||gargoyle||09-03-2001||08:28 PM||||I have one of Archies battery box that I'm about to install. I want to paint it first. Should I prime it with some special paint first or just use any spray type of paint. I'm not looking for pretty, I just want it to blend in better.<BR>Ignore the next two posts, I don't know why this posted 3x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by gargoyle (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||09-03-2001||09:13 PM||||dewax it first or nothing will stick, sand or use a f/g prep wash and a f/g primer then allmost any paint will stick to it.<BR>wax is from mold release and on the surface of the f/g part as a aid to cure it away from air.<BR>even can spray will work ok if good prep.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||09-03-2001||09:58 PM||||Just wash it with a prep solvent. The "Dupli-Color Wax and Grease Remover" works great. Then prime and paint. For the front battery box I would recommend a satin finish. Simular to the trunk panels. A high gloss would look too add-on-ish.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
